        "-m",
        "Namespace compiler snapshot caches by source version\n\nUpstream base: 2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5 with the unchanged\nordered ten-patch compiler stack, head454202b2ba8d0cf10b8caf434a956755e039483f\nand pre-metadata treebae5fe12b58cdf364efeccbabc04cd08205c43b9.\n\nRationale: different compiler snapshots advertising0.1.15 can select the same\npersistent JIT entries when optional library stamping is disabled. Give this\nsnapshot an immutable local package version, used by its existing cache key\nand namespace. The suffix names the pre-metadata source tree, not itself.\n\nQuality: VERSION is the only changed file. Compiler passes, kernels, arithmetic,\nmodels and policies are unchanged. Existing caches are preserved rather than\ncleared or silently reused across compiler identities.\n\nTests: source-only version provider under NO_VERSION_LABEL=1, PEP440/wheel\nparsing, source-derived CMake boundaries and cache-key/namespace disjointness.\nActual Linux wheel/image, installed identity, full release/functional gates\nand both complete metric boots remain required; no serving gain is claimed.\n\nUpstream status: local experiment; not submitted upstream.\n"
